See below.  Nothing is easier to do than pudding farming at this point,
except perhaps Rider farming (and that's because you get a lot more
points for killing a Rider than a pudding).  Rider farming is less
objectionable, I suspect, because by the time you can farm Riders, the
endless pile of score and loot is meaningless for anything beyond its
own sake; the game is long since over, you just haven't offered the
amulet yet.

> The quest home level is one such place.  It's a no-teleport
> level, the quest monsters never go extinct(on the quest) and there is
> only a 14%(IIRC) chance of a different type of monster appearing.  So,
> if you have favorable quest monsters (snakes, bats, wraiths could be
> annoying and a random H could be a formidable titan), you can just
> spam wait and if something dodgy gets generated, then mitigate the
> threat and go back to waiting.

However, with puddings you can spam the splitting, killing, and
sacrificing as well.  People have created bots that do nothing but spam
the split/kill/sac sequences over and over and over again in the
background, and they just keep an eye on things to know when to
interrupt the bot (ie. a titan is randomly generated) and take over
manually for a brief period of time.  Heck, some people just paste a
stock text string into the terminal over and over.

See the difference in effort?  When such a thing is possible, there is a
significant design flaw with the game.*

