* I should clarify here that I am arguing from the perspective of "It
needs fixed in the next version", not "It's cheating if you do this in
3.4.3."  The game is what the game is.  Everyone has access to the same
features; everyone is capable of farming puddings to a greater or lesser
degree, entirely dependent on experience and skill.  As long as pudding
farming is part of the game, it's part of the game, and I don't want to
suggest that I'm implying the past farmers have somehow "cheated"; they
have used the resources available to them.

...That said, however, I'm a fan of well-written and well-designed
software, and the bug that allows pudding farming in the first place
doesn't fall under either of those categories.  It is inelegant design
to create a game in which 75% or more of the game can be bypassed by
simply banging on an imbalance in one feature; and thus, farming should
be fixed.


